## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/dashboard/metrics` | Get dashboard metrics |
| POST | `/api/datasets/upload` | Upload a dataset |
| GET | `/api/datasets` | Get all datasets |
| GET | `/api/datasets/:id` | Get dataset details |
| GET | `/api/datasets/:id/profile` | Get dataset profile |
| POST | `/api/datasets/:id/usage` | Record dataset usage |
| POST | `/api/datasets/:id/scores/refresh` | Refresh governance scores |
| DELETE | `/api/datasets/:id` | Delete dataset |

---

## Installation

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
cd backend
```

### 2. Install dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

### 3. Configure environment variables

Create a `.env` file:

```env
DATABASE_URL=your_postgresql_connection_string
PORT=5000
```

### 4. Generate Prisma Client

```bash
npx prisma generate
```

### 5. Run database migrations

```bash
npx prisma migrate dev
```

### 6. Start the development server

```bash
npm run dev
```

Server runs at:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

---

## Database

### Dataset

Stores uploaded dataset metadata and governance scores.

### DatasetColumn

Stores profiling information for each dataset column.

### DatasetUsage

Stores dataset usage history for analytics.

---

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `DATABASE_URL` | PostgreSQL connection string |
| `PORT` | Application port |
